            <div xml:id="d371">

                <pb facs="0602" n="488" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg488"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15a4/30: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berne</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-01-23T20:00:00+01:00">January 23, 1931—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 23—4:45 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>14. At secret session this afternoon, referred to in my 12, January 23, 11
                        a.m.,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d371-f1"/> members of the Council decided: <list>
                        <label>(1)</label>
                        <item>The General Conference shall meet February 2, 1932;</item>
                        <label>(2)</label>
                        <item>The place shall be Geneva provided adequate facilities are offered as
                            to hotels, meeting places, telegraph lines, et cetera;</item>
                        <label>(3)</label>
                        <item>The chairman of the Conference to be named at a later sitting of the
                            Council (this means not before May);</item>
                        <label>(4)</label>
                        <item>The preparatory work for the General Conference to be carried on by
                            the <hi rendition="#italic">rapporteur</hi> Quiñones de León and the
                            Secretariat between now and the session of the Council in May.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>These decisions are being put in the form of resolutions tonight and it is
                    contemplated they will be submitted to the Council meeting tomorrow morning for
                    formal adoption.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
